## How to Read This

{{#if (eq audience "coach")}}
Written for a **coach**. The tables below are ordered for game preparation: what
the player does most, what beats him, and what to call in a leverage spot. Skip
the rate columns if you are short on time — the usage and location rows carry
the plan.
{{else if (eq audience "gm")}}
Written for a **front office** reader. Emphasis is on acquisition value:
year-over-year direction, workload, and whether the underlying rates support the
surface results. Where a number is small-sample, it is called out rather than
smoothed.
{{else if (eq audience "scout")}}
Written for a **scout**. The data here is meant to be read next to your own
looks, not instead of them. Treat the tables as the statistical half of the
report; the evaluation sections are yours to fill.
{{else}}
Written for an **analyst**. Every figure is reported as bbdata computed it, with
no rounding beyond the display precision shown. Sources are listed in the
footer; re-run the underlying `bbdata query` templates to reproduce any table.
{{/if}}
